 Theorem 4.3 . 
 
 Let A A and B B be finitely generated abelian groups.
If A A is nontrivial and B B is infinite,
then QSP ( A , B , ⋅ , 0 ) {\textsf{QSP}}(A,B,\cdot,0) is 𝐍𝐏 {\mathbf{NP}} -hard. 
 
 
 
 Proof. 
 
 Fix any nontrivial a ∈ A a\in A and any element b ∈ B b\in B of infinite order
(every infinite finitely generated abelian group contains an element of infinite order).
The statement follows immediately from Proposition 4.2 ; the reduction given therein is polynomial-time computable.
