 The bound g ≥ rank ​ ( B ) / 2 g\geq\text{rank}(B)/2 cannot be improved,
i.e., there is a group B B satisfying 2 ​ g < rank ​ ( B ) 2g<\text{rank}(B) for which
the problem is 𝐍𝐏 {\mathbf{NP}} -hard. 
 
 
 Corollary 5.5 . 
 
 Fix g , n ∈ ℕ g,n\in{\mathbb{N}} such that 2 ​ g < n 2g<n .
The Diophantine problem for the class of orientable quadratic
equations ( 2 )
