of genus g g . By Theorem 4.22 , the original problem
 QSP ( ℤ , ℤ n , ⋅ , 2 g ) {\textsf{QSP}}({\mathbb{Z}},{\mathbb{Z}}^{n},\cdot,2g) is 𝐍𝐏 {\mathbf{NP}} -complete.
∎ 
 
 
 
 
 5.1.2. Non-uniform problem: number of conjugates m m 

 
 The number of conjugates m m in a given quadratic equation ℰ {\mathcal{E}} of type ( 2 ) is also responsible for the hardness of solving ℰ {\mathcal{E}} . Specifically, equations ( 2 ) with
 m m bounded by a constant M M can be solved efficiently. 
 
 
 Corollary 5.6 . 
 
 Fix M ∈ ℕ M\in{\mathbb{N}} .
The Diophantine problem for the class of orientable quadratic
equations ( 2 )
with the number of conjugates m m bounded by M M 
over A ≀ B A\wr B is in 𝐏 {\mathbf{P}} . 
 
 
 
 Proof. 
 
 Proposition 3.2 reduces
orientable quadratic equations ( 2 ) in A ≀ B A\wr B satisfying the condition m ≤ M m\leq M to instances of
 QSP ( ⋅ , B , ⋅ | f ¯ | < M , ⋅ ) {\textsf{QSP}}(\cdot,B,\cdot_{|{\overline{f}}|<M},\cdot) , which, by
Theorem 4.24 , are decidable in polynomial time.
